<title>INDIA: India's M3 money supply growth rises to 16.22 pct.</title>
<headline>India's M3 money supply growth rises to 16.22 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth rose to 16.22 percent on August 30, 1996 from 16.15 percent a fortnight ago, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	Aug 30, 1996	 Aug 16, 1996    Sept 1, 1995</p>
<p>	    16.22		16.15	     16.36</p>
<p>Broad money supply was 6,307.42 billion rupees on August 30, 1996 against 6,303.12 billion rupees a fortnight ago and compared to 5,427.05 billion rupees on September 1, 1995, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
